# Vauxhall Chevette four-door saloon, 1975-1984.
#
# Vauxhall's version of the Opel Kadett C "T-car", built at Luton and Ellesmere
# Port: 3,954 mm long, 1,570 mm wide, 1,346 mm high, 2,395 mm wheelbase;
# 1.2-2.3 petrol, the 1256 cc the volume model. Britain's best-selling supermini
# of the late 1970s alongside the Ford Fiesta.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Chevette
#
# Colours: White, Red, Blue and Green are documented Vauxhall colours of the
# period.
#
# Weight: 140 in total (white 45, red 35, blue 35, green 25).
#
# Speed 145 km/h; comfort 65/428 (line). Classes 0,1,2.
# Dates: 1975-1984 with a road tail to about 1995.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-chevette.blend. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-chevette/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia
# Commons.

